      "writtenOn": "2022-08-30T17:35:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So public_deps is a gn thing that means when a target adds this target as a deps, that target can include your public deps in its deps.\n\nSo if you had something A -\u003e(deps) -\u003e B -\u003e(deps) C. Then A would not have anything in C visible to it. However, if you do A -\u003e(deps) -\u003e B -\u003e(public_deps) C, then A would be able to see C.\n\nIn our build the target \"gpu\" needs to be able to see the vulkanmemoryallocator deps (it needs to make sure -I//third_party/vulkanmemoryallocator is on the compile command for its files. since I moved the deps of vma into \"gpu_shared\" I need to set it as a public_deps so that \"gpu\" is still able to see it.",
      "parentUuid": "03ee7e34_253dd102",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 899,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 899,
        "endChar": 17
